"Advanced Construct Summoning": {
  "index": "-97",
  "category": "constructs",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Advanced Construct Summoning",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "I will need to set up a"
        },
        {
          "text": " Construct Gantry",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " and some"
        },
        {
          "text": " Chimerite Crystals",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " in order to modify and summon advanced/more powerful constructs. This setup will allow me to infuse "
        },
        {
          "text": "affinities",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " into the construct, giving it "
        },
        {
          "text": "additional stat boosts",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Setting up the Construct Gantry",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "The requirements for the "
        },
        {
          "text": "Construct Gantry",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " are rather flexible. I'll need the gantry itself, and a total of "
        },
        {
          "text": "8 Chimerite Crystals of any color within 5 blocks",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the workbench in any direction. They can be on walls, ceilings, floors, without line of sight; it doesn't matter."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "location": "mna:textures/guide/construct_workbench.png",
      "width": 120,
      "height": 54
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Summoning the Construct",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Once I have my workbench set up and my parts made, I'll need to choose what "
        },
        {
          "text": "affinities ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "I want to imbue into the construct. \n\nEach "
        },
        {
          "text": "affinity changes attributes of the construct",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". I can set the affinity by casting spells of the given affinity at each of the 8 nearby chimerite crystals. The spells must directly target the crystals, so channeled spells, AoE spells and self spells, for example, will not work. \n\nWhen it works, a sigil will appear above the crystal indicating the affinity. \n\nWhen all five parts of the construct are on the workbench and the 8 affinities are set, I need to activate the workbench itself with an empty hand to begin the crafting process. \n\nOnce the imbuing is complete, I can start to command my construct."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Affinity Effects",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "A construct can have a total of "
        },
        {
          "text": "8 affinity points",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". I've listed below the"
        },
        {
          "text": " effects per point",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " of affinity. "
        },
        {
          "text": "I can mix and match",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " freely, so I should find something that shores up weaknesses within the material used, or enhances the strong points. \n\nConflicting affinities within the construct do not matter.\n\nEach point of affinity also grants the construct limited immunity to damage types related to that affinity, causing it to absorb 1/2 heart of damage per point when attacked."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Air",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ": Faster move speed, +0.25 knockback/point, +1 ranged damage/2 points, kinetic damage resist \n"
        },
        {
          "text": "Arcane",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ": 25% increase in mana capacity per point, magic damage resist \n"
        },
        {
          "text": "Earth",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ": +1 physical damage increase/2 points, +1 armor/point, +1 toughness/2 points, physical damage resist \n"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ender",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ": +1 carry capacity/point for each hand, void/dragon breath damage resist \n"
        },
        {
          "text": "Fire",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ": 1s/point of ignition when attacking, fire/lava/explosion/lightning damage resist \n"
        },
        {
          "text": "Water",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ": +5 buoyancy/point, +4 perception/point, +10% fluid capacity/point, attacks slow targets, frost/drown damage resist"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Swimming"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Constructs can swim if they have a positive buoyancy",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". This is determined by their materials and their affinity. I can see a construct's buoyancy by using the "
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnostics ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "command on a "
        },
        {
          "text": "Bell of Bidding",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
